  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>jbtest</keyword>
  <short_description>Jarque-Bera normality test.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>h = jbtest(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = jbtest(x, alpha)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = jbtest(x, alpha, mctol)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[h, p, jbstat, critval] = jbtest(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>jbtest</b> performs a Jarque-Bera test for normality with unknown mean and variance. <b>NaN</b> observations are omitted.</p>
    <p>The optional <b>alpha</b> argument sets the significance level. The optional <b>mctol</b> argument is accepted for syntax compatibility; this implementation uses the deterministic chi-square approximation.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [1 2 3 4 5];
[h, p, jbstat, critval] = jbtest(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
